Explore Traces' Structure tab issues one query per surface from the template
`({<primary signal>} &>> { <filters> }) || ({<primary signal>}) | select(...)`
against a windowed /api/search. Every emitter-synthetic recursive arm the shape
renders — the two `_struct_closure_*` closures and the `_cerberus_ns_paths`
numbering CTE — must carry the request window as a bare `Timestamp` conjunct on
its own physical `otel_traces` scan, because `otel_traces` is
`PARTITION BY toDate(Timestamp)` and only a predicate on the scan itself prunes
partitions: a windowed `TraceId IN (<seed>)` membership is inert (#1109).

The lane proves that twice over. The `-- sql --` golden records the conjunct
literally, and the post-optimizer re-emit runs `chsql.GuardEmittedSQL`, which
rejects any recursive arm reading `otel_traces` without a co-scope `Timestamp`
predicate — so a fixture here fails the moment the predicate goes missing or
the guard stops recognising it (#1889).

`select(status)` names no nested-set attribute, so no numbering CTE is built.
The `&>>` closure arms remain, and they are windowed on their own scans.

-- search_limit --
20
-- search_window --
1782571392 1782573192
-- query.traceql --
({ true } &>> { }) || ({ true }) | select(status)
-- seed --
CREATE TABLE otel_traces (
    TraceId String,
    SpanId String,
    ParentSpanId String,
    SpanName String,
    SpanKind String,
    Duration Int64,
    Timestamp DateTime64(9),
    StatusCode String,
    StatusMessage String,
    ScopeName String,
    ScopeVersion String,
    SpanAttributes Map(String, String),
    ResourceAttributes Map(String, String)
) ENGINE = MergeTree ORDER BY (Timestamp, SpanId);
INSERT INTO otel_traces VALUES
    ('a0000000000000000000000000000001', '1000000000000001', '', 'root', 'Server', 300, toDateTime64('2026-06-27 14:50:00.000000001', 9), 'Unset', '', '', '', map(), map()),
    ('a0000000000000000000000000000001', '1000000000000002', '1000000000000001', 'child', 'Client', 200, toDateTime64('2026-06-27 14:50:00.000000002', 9), 'Error', '', '', '', map(), map()),
    ('a0000000000000000000000000000001', '1000000000000003', '1000000000000002', 'grandchild', 'Server', 100, toDateTime64('2026-06-27 14:50:00.000000003', 9), 'Unset', '', '', '', map(), map()),
    ('b0000000000000000000000000000001', '2000000000000001', '', 'root', 'Server', 300, toDateTime64('2026-06-27 14:51:00.000000001', 9), 'Unset', '', '', '', map(), map()),
    ('b0000000000000000000000000000001', '2000000000000002', '2000000000000001', 'child', 'Client', 200, toDateTime64('2026-06-27 14:51:00.000000002', 9), 'Unset', '', '', '', map(), map());
